\title{Formalized Theoretical Intelligence Potential}
\tag{notes}
\tag{math}
\tag{draft}
\tag{agent-draft}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{language-model}
\tag{reinforcement-learning}

\author{utensil}
\date{2026-08-27}

\p{These research notes study \strong{Formalized Theoretical Intelligence
Potential} (FTIP): how much task-relevant capability post-training can elicit
or acquire from a language model, and how that gain depends on the model,
feedback, reward design, optimization, rollout compute, sandbox compute, and
deployment-time inference. “Potential” is therefore not a single intrinsic
number attached to a model. It is a conditional frontier indexed by a task law
and a protocol.}

\p{The first draft is deliberately introductory. It begins with the object
being trained and the process that creates its base distribution, then follows
the transition from supervised post-training to reinforcement learning with
verifiable rewards (RLVR). Only after that context does it introduce tasks,
environments, histories, policies, feedback, credit, and costed potential.}

\p{The recurring mechanism spine is the following. The diagram is
\strong{schematic}: each arrow will later become a typed map or stochastic
kernel, and each cost label will become part of the lifecycle budget.}

\tikzfig{\begin{tikzpicture}[
  node distance=8mm,
  every node/.style={draw, rounded corners=2pt, align=center,
    text width=29mm, minimum height=11mm},
  every path/.style={-{Stealth[length=2mm]}, thick}
]
\node (base) {architecture, data,\\and pretraining};
\node[right=of base] (post) {post-training\\protocol};
\node[right=of post] (agent) {agentic rollout\\and environment};
\node[right=of agent] (eval) {independent\\evaluation};
\draw (base) -- node[draw=none, above=5mm, text width=18mm] {base policy} (post);
\draw (post) -- node[draw=none, above=5mm, text width=18mm] {current policy} (agent);
\draw (agent) -- node[draw=none, above=5mm, text width=18mm] {outcomes} (eval);
\draw[bend right=33, dashed] (agent.south) to
  node[draw=none, below=7mm, text width=30mm] {feedback, reward, credit} (post.south);
\end{tikzpicture}}

\p{Definitions in this suite are working research interfaces rather than
claims that one paper has supplied the final ontology. Each definition is
followed by a remark recording the literatures it reconciles, the distinctions
it preserves, and the questions or theorem families it is meant to support.}

